/-!
# The monomial and nonmonomial parts of an ideal along a submanifold

Let `N` be a closed submanifold, `E` a simple normal crossings divisor transverse to `N` (`n > 0`), and `𝔞` a coherent
ideal.  The exponents `e_i = divExpAlong 𝔞 N E_i` are those of `DivisorExponentAlong`.

* **Adapted retraction** (`flatRetract`, `isLocalRetraction_flatRetract`): in coordinates in which `N = ℂ^{k_N} × 0`
  (`BlowupSNCTransform.IsAdaptedAt n N N E x`), the flat retraction `φ ∘ P ∘ ψ` is a local retraction onto `N` which
  keeps the coordinates of index `< k_N`, hence maps each member through `x` into itself
  (`exists_isLocalRetraction_preserving`).
* **Simultaneous divisibility along `N`** (`exists_eq_mul_prod_of_forall_along`): a germ whose restriction to `N` is
  divisible by each `u_i^{a_i}` (`u_i` the coordinate of a member, of index `< k_N`) is divisible on `N` by the product;
  the retracted germ `g ∘ r` is divisible by each `u_i^{a_i}` ambiently, and `MonomialPart.exists_eq_mul_prod_of_forall`
  applies to it.
* `monomialPartAlong` (`𝓜_N`): at `y ∈ N`, the germs whose restriction to `N` lies in `(𝓘_{E_i}^{e_i(y)})|_N` for every
  member through `y` (every germ off `N`); `le_monomialPartAlong`: `𝔞 ⊆ 𝓜_N`.
* `monomialPartAlong_mem_iff`: near `x ∈ N`, `𝓜_N` restricted to `N` is generated by `m = ∏_{x ∈ E_i} u_i^{e_i(x)}`,
  which vanishes identically on no relatively open subset of `N` (`frequently_generator_ne_zero`); this is the `hgen`
  form of `MonomialBlowupAlongChart.exists_snc_chart_geoTransform_along_of_flat`.
* `nonmonomialPartAlong` (`𝓝_N = (Res_N 𝔞 : 𝓜_N)`, `RestrictedIdealQuotient.colonAlong`): `restrictLe_mul_along`,
  `restrictLe_mul_along'`: `Res_N 𝔞 = Res_N (𝓜_N 𝓝_N)`; `exists_mem_nonmonomialPartAlong_not`: at a point of `N ∩ E_i`
  some germ of `𝓝_N` does not restrict into `(𝓘_{E_i})|_N`.
* `isCoherent_monomialPartAlong`, `isCoherent_nonmonomialPartAlong`.
* `IsMonomialAlong` (`Res_N 𝓜_N ⊆ Res_N 𝔞`) and `isInSpanOnAt_iff_generator_of_isMonomialAlong`: for a monomial
  ideal along `N` the restricted stalk at `x` is generated by `∏_{x ∈ E_i} w_{σ i}^{e_i(x)}` -- the input of
  monomial chart along `N'`, for the monomial case along `N`.
-/

open Set Filter
open scoped Topology Manifold ContDiff

